course: dictionary
lesson: 8054
title: Reign: rule, time, and strongest feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reign is a word with two jobs: a verb (to reign) and a noun (a reign). The words around it show you which meaning fits. «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, 1661–1722, the longest reign in Chinese history.» Here reign is a noun: it is the length of time a ruler sits on the throne.
explain: «Queen Elizabeth II reigned for 70 years, from 1952 to 2022.» Try the swap check: put ruled in place of reigned and the sentence still makes sense. So to reign means to rule as a king, queen or emperor.
explain: Reign can also mean being the strongest or most noticeable thing in a place. «Silence reigned» means silence was everywhere. «Chaos reigned» means everything was in a mess. Ask yourself: is a person in charge here? If not, the word means something is the strongest thing around.
explain: In sport, the reigning champion is the one who won last time and still holds the title. Look at the clues: the word champion tells you it is about winning, and the word reigning tells you the title is still held now.
fact: To reign means to rule as a king, queen or emperor; a reign is the time they rule.
fact: «The Kangxi Emperor ruled 61 years, 1661–1722, the longest reign in Chinese history.»
fact: «Queen Elizabeth II reigned for 70 years, from 1952 to 2022, longer than any other British monarch.»
fact: «Silence reigned» means silence was the strongest thing in a place; «chaos reigned» means everything was in a mess.
fact: The reigning champion is the one who won last time and still holds the title.
exercise: «Queen Elizabeth II reigned for 70 years.» What does reigned mean here? | Stopped working | *Ruled as queen | Stayed indoors | Won a race
exercise: «The Edwardian age is the reign of King Edward VII, from 1901 to 1910.» What does reign mean in this sentence? | *The time a king rules | A building where a king lives | A kind of crown | A war between two countries
exercise: «Silence reigned in the library after the bell.» What does reigned suggest? | The bell was ringing again | *Silence was everywhere, the strongest thing in the room | Everyone ran outside | People were singing loudly
test: «The reigning champion walked onto the court, sure of winning again.» What does reigning champion mean? | The player who lost the last game | A new player who has never played before | *The player who won last time and still holds the title | The referee
test: «Ethiopia's last emperor, Haile Selassie, had a reign that ended in 1974.» What is a reign in this sentence? | A kind of Ethiopian food | The name of his palace | *The time he ruled as emperor | A list of his children
exam: «Chaos reigned in the classroom when the lights went out.» What does reigned mean? | Went home early | Was very quiet and calm | Sat down at the front | *Was everywhere, with everything in a mess
